d States&#8217; nuclear weapons enterprise has wrestled with an institutional paradox. On one hand is the imperative to make the complex more &#8220;responsive&#8221; to global tumult and technical sur', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/this-is-not-your-fathers-nuclear-flight-test-vehicle/'}, {'signal_id': '144f18951d48a536', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Big Bet on the Emerging Space Economy <p>The space economy has surpassed $600 billion in annual value, with some projecting it will reach a trillion by the 2030s. Jonathan Panter is joined by Joseph Yaffe (Cowboy Space), Brian Weeden (The Aerospace Corporation), and Dan Wald ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-big-bet-on-the-emerging-space-economy/'}, {'signal_id': '572beec097ba7921', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Age of Strategic Exclusion <p>Major powers are increasingly trying to shut out their rivals. Russia invaded Ukraine in part to prevent the latter&#8217;s further integration with the West. The United States is restricting China&#8217;s access to advanced semiconductors and en', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-age-of-strategic-exclusion/'}, {'signal_id': 'f0fc561dabb21987', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The War’s Last Generation Is Still Holding America’s Moral Debt <p>On the first night of the evacuation of Kabul, Aug. 15, 2021, a young mother found me in the crowd at Hamid Karzai International Airport. She had marked me, correctly, as someone who spoke her language. By the end', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-wars-last-generation-is-still-holding-americas-moral-debt/'}, {'signal_id': '4b88f91f1e94cc8a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'What America’s Adversaries and Allies Hope to Gain at the U.N. General Assembly <p>This year&#8217;s U.N. General Assembly officially opened on Tuesday, Sept. 8. The annual gathering gives diplomats and leaders a valuable opportunity to press their foreign policy priorities and e', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/what-americas-adversaries-and-allies-hope-to-gain-at-the-u-n-general-assembly/'}, {'signal_id': 'a7390c5588471bb5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Automating the Action Officer: Between Bureaucracy and Technology <p>If there is a revolution brewing in the automation of white-collar work, you wouldn&#8217;t know it at the Pentagon. Here, the typical action officers, staff who tackle the daily work of the bureaucracy, perform', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/automating-the-action-officer-between-bureaucracy-and-technology/'}, {'signal_id': '0b26e2a94a596635', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Assessment Gap in U.S. Counter-Terrorism Strikes <p>For eight years I helped decide whether American counter-terrorism money was working.As a programs advisor in the State Department&#8217;s Bureau of Counterterrorism from 2018 to 2025, I oversaw about 20 projects in East Afr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-assessment-gap-in-u-s-counter-terrorism-strikes/'}, {'signal_id': '2d8abdb2b2846625', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Forced Into the Right Decision? A Look at U.S. Land-Based Deterrence Posture <p>In 2019, Steve Fetter wrote &#8220;A Cheaper Nuclear Sponge,&#8221; in which he argued that building a new intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) was unnecessary for strengthening U.S. land-based d', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/forced-into-the-right-decision-a-look-at-u-s-land-based-deterrence-posture/'}, {'signal_id': '2636724d659b320b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Coming Age of Robotic Warfare <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/france-defence-army-weaponry.jpg?id=68580393&amp;width=1200&amp;height=400&amp;coordinates=0%2C171%2C0%2C171" /><br /><br /><p>A battalion of armed robots moves against a unit of soldiers, ai', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-coming-age-of-robotic-warfare'}, {'signal_id': 'b0f661e1d265e2e1', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Fire Base Australia: Can America’s Southern Base Sustain a Pacific War? <p>American access to Australian bases is only as valuable as Australia’s ability to keep them operating under attack. For Washington, <a href="https://www.defence.gov.au/defence-activities/programs-initiativ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/fire-base-australia-can-americas-southern-base-sustain-a-pacific-war'}, {'signal_id': 'e23071c10fb2f7e7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Hidden Cost of America’s War With Iran <p>“The [U.S. Naval Support Activity Bahrain] base and Fifth Fleet headquarters have been rendered largely inoperable for their original functions, with repairs estimated at $400 million… Chief of Naval Operations Admiral Daryl Caudle an', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hidden-cost-war-with-iran'}, {'signal_id': 'dd10d7b644f8a031', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Command We Must Start <p><strong></strong>In 1928, Secretary of War Dwight Davis ordered the Army to assemble an experimental mechanized force of tanks, armored cars, and motorized infantry at Camp Meade, Maryland. It was disbanded within months. A second attempt was dissolve', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-command-we-must-start'}, {'signal_id': '43f6f5be3435ac91', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Cipher Brief’s 10th Threat Conference: Optimism, Urgency, and the Imperative to Act <p>Which came first: The Cloister at Sea Island, the Office of Strategic Services, or the CIA? The resort wins. The Cloister first opened in 1928, fourteen years before the OSS and nineteen be', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-cipher-briefs-10th-threat-conference-optimism-urgency-and-the-imperative-to-act'}, {'signal_id': '6114ee09bd6fceae', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Kids are Alright: U.S. Soft Power, Aid, and Youth in Africa <p><em>OPINION — A recent survey of African youth challenges conventional wisdom on foreign aid. Policymakers should take heed of their views as they design the future of U.S. foreign assistance to increase effective', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-kids-are-alright'}, {'signal_id': 'c6ca6333ccf272ad', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "F-35 Fallacy: Jets Alone Will Not Save Us <p>NATO Allies have bet the future of European skies on the world’s most sophisticated combat aircraft. NATO Allies are buying the world's most advanced fighter but many are neglecting vital investments in hard security, ground crews, and", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/f-35-fallacy-jets-alone-will-not-save-us'}, {'signal_id': 'fee7d3e35b4d3134', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Military Has Much to Learn From Ukraine <p>“What does Ukraine really need? How do we make sure they're delivering what they actually need? And you know, right now those are air defense munitions, it's funding for drones, it's extended range artillery, electronic warfare,", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/why-americas-military-still-needs-its-allies'}, {'signal_id': '1a2041754d6a8495', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Terms We Must Set <p>On October 23, Russia's deputy prime minister said three tankers were at sea, that supply contracts were being finalized, and that volumes would rise to 1 million tons in December and could reach 3 million a month. A week earlier, the United States had wa", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-terms-we-must-set'}, {'signal_id': '15cbfb74f4b66b65', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Thirteenth Mile: This Is What Gray Zone War Looks Like <p>On the morning of October 23, the cargo ship Khoryv sent a distress call <a href="https://www.kyivpost.com/post/88003" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">13 nautical miles off Constanța</a>, Romania. Territorial', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-thirteenth-mile-this-is-what-gray-zone-war-looks-like'}, {'signal_id': '2bbcaebde45ce997', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Intelligence Community’s Missing Discipline <p>Economic statecraft has become a primary instrument of US national security, deployed with a frequency and ambition that outpaces the intelligence architecture built to support it. For sanctions, tariffs, investment screening, ex', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-intelligence-communitys-missing-discipline'}, {'signal_id': '535c3685a554e588', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'We’re Losing the Cognitive Space Race <p>Over the last century, modern medicine achieved a historic feat. We increased the human lifespan by 33%. But at the same time, we completely failed to defend our brain healthspan. Today, a silent gap of 15 to 30 years exists between the ti', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/were-losing-the-cognitive-space-race'}, {'signal_id': '4b15e2360fb8530e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Russia Never Left the International Financial System. It Built a Way Back In. <p>A7’s OpenAI prompt was six words long: "Translate [name] to [language]. Answer only translated text."</p><p>Developer code leaked in 2025 from A7—the Kremlin-linked payment network designated by Trea', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/russia-never-left-the-international-financial-system-it-built-a-way-back-in'}, {'signal_id': 'fcc142ead8a66abb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Turkey Has Outsourced Its Censorship to American Companies <p>Earlier this month, Sky News correspondent <a href="https://ground.news/article/sky-news-reporter-alex-crawfords-x-account" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Alex Crawford</a> got a notice from X: her account w', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/turkey-has-outsourced-its-censorship-to-american-companies'}, {'signal_id': 'e1b2c0d145ded66c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Technology Is Outrunning the Way We Fight <p>The United States is racing to field AI and autonomous systems. It is not racing to figure out how to fight with them. This imbalance between technology and concepts is widening a gap the U.S. is ill prepared to close. Ukraine has show', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/technology-is-outrunning-the-way-we-fight'}, {'signal_id': '15b847110bac0873', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Hybrid Threats: Why Awareness Must Transcend Individual Cyberattacks <p>Every October, Cybersecurity Awareness Month puts practical security measures in the spotlight. Can an employee recognize a phishing email? Will someone pause before clicking a suspicious link? Are passwords ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hybrid-threats-why-awareness-must-transcend-individual-cyberattacks'}, {'signal_id': '46024bc6e9fc668a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America\'s Counter-Drone Authority Is Real, The Capacity Isn\'t Yet <p>Here is a number worth sitting with: federal teams seized roughly <a href="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fbi-counter-drone-school-double-capacity-woodward" target="_blank" title="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fb', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/america-s-counter-drone-authority-is-real-the-capacity-isn-t-yet'}, {'signal_id': '217c50e76268bc84', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Army’s Pacific Strategy Depends on Allies <p>“We never fight alone. We've never done that. You can go all the way back to the days of Revolutionary War. The United States has never gone into conflict on its own. We've always built coalitions. We've always involved partne", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-u-s-armys-pacific-strategy-depends-on-allies'}, {'signal_id': '612051baeeba5542', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Hidden Risks of AI-Powered Intelligence <p><span>Picture an </span>intelligent analyst's screen. Data about troop movements, a port closure, a terrorist attack, or a weapons transfer sits at the center of a clean interface, with a confidence indicator glowing green. Two hundr", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-hidden-risks-of-ai-powered-intelligence'}, {'signal_id': '67fbdeb10f8d3e21', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What a Russian Hybrid Attack Might Look Like <p>Russia has demonstrated a growing willingness to use hybrid tactics – including sabotage, cyberattacks, information operations, and the use of deniable or “throwaway” agents – to create disruption and uncertainty across Europe. This', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-a-russian-hybrid-attack-might-look-like'}, {'signal_id': 'aabdf5a0d915c66e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Muhammad bin Salman’s Humbling and the Return of the Ottomans <p>The Houthis bloodied Saudi Crown Prince Muhammad bin Salman’s nose—again—with their deadly, cruel, but effective attacks on Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport last week. The strikes are the latest in a serie', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/muhammad-bin-salmans-humbling-and-the-return-of-the-ottomans'}, {'signal_id': '1768a2a205f8c24a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Day We Cannot Choose <p>Washington made three decisions this week, and none of them has an end date. On the night of October 14, Ukrainian units in the field found that their Starshield terminals had been capped at a speed, 160 kilometers an hour by the published figure, 70 b', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-day-we-cannot-choose'}, {'signal_id': '809453e0a348c58b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How Far Should the U.S. Go to Defend Saudi Arabia? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/saudi-yemen-us-israel-iran-war.jpg?id=68454050&amp;width=1200&amp;height=400&amp;coordinates=0%2C170%2C0%2C171" /><br /><br /><p><em>Recent deadly attacks by Yemen\'s Iranian-', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-far-should-the-u-s-go-to-defend-saudi-arabia'}, {'signal_id': 'b097fb4beb88b6eb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Who Really Makes Decisions in Tehran? <p>Ayatollah Ali Khamenei’s death led to greater decentralization of the regime and a more collective, securitized decision-making system. In Iran today, authority is distributed across several actors and groups, in which the military-securit', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/who-really-makes-decisions-in-tehran'}, {'signal_id': 'd5f29eddafe9987c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Soviet Roots of Russia’s Modern Disinformation War <p>Anti-Semitism, the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. pronounced while repudiating an anti-Israel resolution adopted at the 1967 National <a href="https://www.jta.org/archive/dr-king-repudiates-anti-semitic-anti-israel-black-', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-soviet-roots-of-russias-modern-disinformation-war'}, {'signal_id': 'e217dc903f365fe4', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Europe’s Changing Politics and the Future of U.S. Leadership <p>“And now, there is war again. There is new competition between great powers. There is vulnerability, aggression, terrorism, a whole universe of new threats and attacks again. And so, we must rebuild our institutions ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/europes-changing-politics-and-the-future-of-u-s-leadership'}, {'signal_id': 'c5b36c915fd20f4c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What Beijing Calls Open, Washington Should Call an Operation <p><em>China is about to run the largest influence operation in history. It will not have to run it. The world will download it.</em><em></em></p><p><strong>EXPERT PERSPECTIVE</strong> -- Our research team at Vanderbilt', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-beijing-calls-open-washington-should-call-an-operation-2678089778'}, {'signal_id': '2e00ae1d8820c2c2', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Washington Cannot Outsource Saudi Security to the Mecca Pact <p>The Houthis have significantly escalated their airstrike campaign targeting civilian infrastructure in Saudi Arabia, with <a href="https://apnews.com/article/saudi-yemen-houthi-riyadh-airport-d2e0868ffb18d883c16465d7', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/washington-cannot-outsource-saudi-security-to-the-mecca-pact'}, {'signal_id': '3f263fbed8d41717', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Next War of Attrition is in Yemen <p>Battlefield dynamics in Yemen shift quickly, but Houthi aims do not. A movement organized around radical ideology and perpetual conflict now shares a border with a state organized around modernization and prosperity. Saudi Arabia and the H', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-next-war-of-attrition-is-in-yemen'}, {'signal_id': '5fb5d97689873bb8', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Pentagon’s Drone Revolution Starts With Soldiers <p><strong><em>Welcome to The Iron Triangle, the Cipher Brief column serving Procurement Officers tasked with buying the future, Investors funding the next generation of defense technology, and the Policy Wonks analyzing its im', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-pentagons-drone-revolution-starts-with-soldiers'}, {'signal_id': 'fd64b2d7c06c6f6e', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Guantanamo Dispatches: Jury Selection Is Underway in the USS Cole Bombing Case, First Capital Case at Guantanamo Bay <p>Jury selection began Monday in the trial of the USS Cole Bombing suspect, the first death penalty trial to be held at Guantanamo.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163180/jury-selection-uss-cole-bombing-trial-guantanamo/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=jury-selection-uss-cole-bombing-trial-guantanamo'}, {'signal_id': '5bdaa52a2574d15f', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'John Eastman’s Most Dangerous Supreme Court Case Yet <p>A ruling restoring Eastman\'s law license after it was revoked for his efforts to overturn the 2020 election would weaken the rule of law.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162149/john-eastman-most-dangero', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162149/john-eastman-most-dangerous-supreme-court-case/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=john-eastman-most-dangerous-supreme-court-case'}, {'signal_id': 'a0e43217578f5c9f', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Series: Comparing National Trends in Cyber and Surveillance Expansion <p>Introducing a series on the expansion of cyber and surveillance powers convened by the Atlantic Council in partnership with Just Security.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/161321/trends-', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161321/trends-cyber-surveillance-expansion/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=trends-cyber-surveillance-expansion'}, {'signal_id': 'd1f6fa23b9b2c5b1', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Accountability Will Come – What Should It Look Like for the Department of Defense? <p>Failing to hold leaders accountable for the abuses of the Trump administration\'s Pentagon would invite future officials to repeat them.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/1621', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162162/accountability-will-come-department-of-defense/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=accountability-will-come-department-of-defense'}, {'signal_id': '6d777451dab37427', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: November 3, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR The United States yesterday attacked Iran’s Qeshm Island, U.S. officials told t', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/163177/early-edition-november-3-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-november-3-2026'}, {'signal_id': '71251dc4c0815961', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Litigation Tracker: Legal Challenges to Trump Administration Actions <p>A public resource tracking all the legal challenges to the Trump administration\'s executive orders and actions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration'}, {'signal_id': 'ac9bd54c7dcdfaa4', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': '2026 Midterms: Election Integrity Litigation Tracker <p>A tracker of major litigation concerning the integrity of the 2026 midterm elections.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162830/2026-midterms-election-integrity-litigation-tracker/">2026 Midterms: Election', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162830/2026-midterms-election-integrity-litigation-tracker/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=2026-midterms-election-integrity-litigation-tracker'}, {'signal_id': '9db39ef5ff360ad3', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Constitutional Collision Course <p>How Congress can help bolster federal judges and help stop Trump administration noncompliance with court orders.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162909/constitutional-collision-course/">Constitutional Collision Course</a> a', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162909/constitutional-collision-course/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=constitutional-collision-course'}, {'signal_id': '8f64f47f9e85663b', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Questions for Congress: AI in Targeting and Civilian Protection <p>What Congress should ask Defense Department officials about its use of AI for targeting and the protections in place against civilian harm.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/161298/ai-targeting', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161298/ai-targeting-civilian-protection-congress-questions/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=ai-targeting-civilian-protection-congress-questions'}, {'signal_id': 'd0ae425af73dbf5e', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Lula’s Army: Lessons From Online Political Mobilization <p>Lula\'s victory last week carries a lesson about how online political mobilization can be a powerful tool for pro-democracy movements.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/162755/lulas-army-lessons-online-', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/162755/lulas-army-lessons-online-political-mobilization/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=lulas-army-lessons-online-political-mobilization'}, {'signal_id': '2a2e2626dbe7e57d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Lessons from L.A. on Transfer Taxes San Francisco voters have a new proposition on real estate transfer taxes to consider. Aspects of and arguments for the new Prop 1 closely mirror the debate over Los Angeles' Measure ULA, a 2022 ballot initiative that established a similar tran", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/lessons-from-la-on-transfer-taxes.html'}, {'signal_id': 'fa820f34bcc199f0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Employers Can't Tame Health Costs Price transparency alone isn’t helping employers rein in health care costs. What will it take to give them real leverage—and overcome the barriers of today’s system?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/why-employers-cant-tame-health-costs.html'}, {'signal_id': '27c968e09255c3ca', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "America's Least Bad Option in Iran In Iran, the United States could return to a full-scale bombing campaign, walk away from the conflict, or stick with the current approach. Staying the course almost certainly will not bring quick results but it is strategically prudent.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/americas-least-bad-option-in-iran.html'}, {'signal_id': '1360f15fbaf3d074', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Quick Compensation Hasn't Replaced Eaton Fire Lawsuits—So Far A review of Southern California Edison's direct-payment program finds that it has paid claimants much faster, but it hasn't become a broad substitute for lawsuits.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/why-quick-compensation-hasnt-replaced-eaton-fire-lawsuits.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e2180ad066e052', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Link in Drug Policy: Why Whole-System Reform Is Stalling The UK has made progress toward a whole-system approach to drug policy, but unclear accountability and persistent stigma are stalling reform.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/the-missing-link-in-drug-policy-why-whole-system-reform.html'}, {'signal_id': '1c27b342495b14b7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "A Better Way to Use Criminal Records in Hiring Employers want to know whether an applicant is likely to commit another crime, possibly on the job. But the screening rules many of them use are often about as accurate as a coin toss, in part because they're based on data that don't", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/a-better-way-to-use-criminal-records-in-hiring.html'}, {'signal_id': '1f82f8da9de912b0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Biosecurity in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Steph Guerra The question that drives Steph Guerra's work at RAND may be one of the most consequential for this moment in the AI era: How can we harness the full potential of AI for science and medicine—but also ensure it never helps any", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/biosecurity-in-the-age-of-ai-qa-with-steph-guerra.html'}, {'signal_id': '510596eafa31042f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'From Strategic Logic to Practical Implementation: A Phased Agenda for U.S.-ROK Shipbuilding Cooperation U.S.-ROK cooperation on shipbuilding should be structured so that it strengthens U.S. maritime industrial capacity, makes commercial sense for Korean shipbuilders, and survives', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/from-strategic-logic-to-practical-implementation-a.html'}, {'signal_id': 'c5904b48ce512115', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "9/11's Forgotten Lesson Twenty-five years later, 9/11's lessons are still contested, except the simplest: the United States mistook quiet for peace. And it is doing so again.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/911s-forgotten-lesson.html'}, {'signal_id': '645e5c8159c45b3c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Schools, Cell Phones, and AI: Q&amp;A with Melissa Kay Diliberti Melissa Kay Diliberti, an associate policy researcher at RAND, discusses recent findings from RAND that can help parents and policymakers better understand what challenges schools are up against.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/schools-cell-phones-and-ai-qa-with-melissa-kay-diliberti.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f0a6bf01926bc40a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Netanyahu May Have Ignored a Dire Warning. Israel Ignores the Deeper Threat. Israel's strategy in Gaza is only keeping Hamas in power: deterred, but not replaced, with no real alternative given a chance. A different outcome calls for a different approach.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/nentanyahu-may-have-ignored-a-dire-warning-israel-ignores-the.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b489a15858be84c1', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Never Underestimate the Houthis Yemen's Houthi rebels are in a position to shape the next phase of the conflict between the United States and Iran if they attempt to renew their blockade of the Bab al-Mandab Strait. And no one should assume that a deal with Iran will bind what th", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/never-underestimate-the-houthis.html'}, {'signal_id': '19d8064c433770cf', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Preserving Jobs and Tax Revenue in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Carter Price Carter Price, a mathematician at RAND and co-director of the RAND Von Furstenberg Family Budget Model Initiative, discusses ways to rebalance the tax code so that it doesn't incentivize employers to repla", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/preserving-jobs-and-tax-revenue-in-the-age-of-ai-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2d02311d1d9e0e7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Recent Rise of Women Gun Owners In recent years, women made up almost half of all new gun owners, a striking shift from the historical norm, when women accounted for about a quarter of them. And the uptick is widespread across geographic and demographic subgroups.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/the-recent-rise-of-women-gun-owners.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a9dc8988cf7146c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Who Benefits from Education Savings Accounts? Q&amp;A with Susha Roy Tens of thousands of American families use state-funded education savings accounts for their children's education. How exactly do these accounts work? Who benefits from them? And how do they affect education fun", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/who-benefits-from-education-savings-accounts.html'}, {'signal_id': '480b7da85115059d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Getting a Security Clearance Doesn't Have to Be So Intimidating: Q&amp;A with Sina Beaghley The security clearance process can be difficult and time-consuming but the government has made big strides in improving it. Sina Beaghley, a senior international and defense researcher at ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/getting-a-security-clearance-doesnt-have-to-be-so-intimidating.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2b8719ed5ca0a96', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': '25 Years After 9/11: Lessons for Securing the Homeland Reflecting on 25 years since the September 11 terror attacks, RAND experts answer questions about protecting soft targets, the role of the TSA, mitigating risks from emerging technologies, and more.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/25-years-after-911-lessons-for-securing-the-homeland.html'}, {'signal_id': '080553cfaf2bb84f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'AI Can Now Design Viruses. We Need Biosecurity Guardrails Now As AI advances, the risk of engineered viral bioweapons is growing. The window to prepare is now—by building a layered, resilient system of defense.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/ai-can-now-design-viruses-we-need-biosecurity-guardrails.html'}, {'signal_id': '20bc7f624125f201', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Tomorrow's Victory and the Army of the Future: Forecasting the Next Steps in Ukraine's Military Evolution Ukraine’s military has changed substantially since Russia’s full-scale invasion in 2022. Will its next evolution be shaped by traditionalists or technologists?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/tomorrows-victory-and-the-army-of-the-future.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f540d78c60af3817', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'When Disaster Strikes, Could AI Help? Q&amp;A with Jessica Jensen Disasters are more frequent, more severe, and more costly. Pressure is mounting on emergency managers and the organizations that support them. Senior policy researcher Jessica Jensen discusses how artificial intell', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/when-disaster-strikes-could-ai-help-qa-with-jessica.html'}, {'signal_id': '48c0a4431fdad63a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Religion as statecraft: What a decade of research reveals about the geopolitics of religious soft power <p>The post-Cold War assumption that international politics was converging toward a secular liberal framework in which religion would play at most a marginal role has not survi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/religion-as-statecraft-what-a-decade-of-research-reveals-about-the-geopolitics-of-religious-soft-power/'}, {'signal_id': '2f21c01cb61a67c8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Abu Dhabi: America votes—and the world holds its breath <p>The world is showing more interest than ever in the US midterm elections, and with good reason given how the results could affect Trump\'s foreign policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dispatch-from-abu-dhabi-america-votes-and-the-world-holds-its-breath/'}, {'signal_id': '5ad7af3ef0557cfc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Scowcroft Strategy Scorecard: Grading Canada’s second-ever national security strategy <p>For only the second time in its history, Canada has a new national security strategy. Does it match the clarity with which Prime Minister Mark Carney has described the challenges the country ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/scorecard/scowcroft-strategy-scorecard-grading-canadas-second-ever-national-security-strategy/'}, {'signal_id': '305d78c1be93e255', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Iran War: What Victory Must Achieve. <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-iran-war-what-victory-must-achieve/">Charai for The Jerusalem Strate', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-iran-war-what-victory-must-achieve/'}, {'signal_id': '3f21234d817e4e7a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How to prevent an energy quarantine of Taiwan <p>An all-of-the-above energy strategy in Taiwan can help the United States and allies deter a Chinese energy quarantine of the island.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how-to-prevent-an-energy-quarantine-of-taiwan/'}, {'signal_id': '72a3e6dde5a2e9ab', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As energy prices threaten inflation again, Lagarde’s European Central Bank legacy offers lessons <p>Christine Lagarde\'s European Central Bank legacy reflects strong crisis management and efforts to strengthen the euro, but a mixed record on inflation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="htt', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/as-energy-prices-threaten-inflation-again-lagardes-european-central-bank-legacy-offers-lessons/'}, {'signal_id': 'c5f106fd0eb26daa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Washington Tariff & Trade Letter on the US’s use of Smoot-Hawley law to impose tariffs on Canada <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-on-the-uss-use-of-smoot-hawley-law-to-impose-tariffs-on-canada/'}, {'signal_id': '8b2a0910ab390025', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in National Post on the implications of USMCA uncertainty on long-term North American supply chain security <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-im', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-implications-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-long-term-north-american-supply-chain-security/'}, {'signal_id': '5544debd93d9e27e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Reforma on how China benefits from USMCA uncertainty and fragmentation <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-fragmentation/'}, {'signal_id': 'd6db0