es-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-3/'}, {'signal_id': 'd68ead9a82c828af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'De Kruijf cited in National Interest article on the Trump administration’s policy toward the International Criminal Court (ICC) <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-bloomberg-article-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-bloomberg-article-on-the-impact-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-supply-chains-2/'}, {'signal_id': '815479d013ed2eca', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Trump will define his legacy through Russia—one way or the other <p>The US president inherited Russia’s war on Ukraine, but he will own the consequences of how it ends.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-will-define-his', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-will-define-his-legacy-through-russia-one-way-or-the-other/'}, {'signal_id': '7c96f28b319b0b20', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukrainians are not fighting for Zelenskyy. They are fighting for national survival. <p>Trump and Putin both seem to think that removing Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy would set the stage for a Kremlin-friendly peace deal, but most Ukrainians see the war as a fight for na', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukrainians-are-not-fighting-for-zelenskyy-they-are-fighting-for-survival/'}, {'signal_id': 'e1aa97b5e500a1d3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The new Middle East is modular <p>In the Middle East today, states are aligning issue by issue, not choosing sides. They cooperate in one area and compete in the next. This modular alignment is shaping the region, even as it manages the shocks of war and energy-market volatility.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/the-big-story/the-new-middle-east-is-modular/'}, {'signal_id': '031868c41e60b35a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in The Sun on potential attacks on undersea infrastructure <p>On October 17, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed in The Sun to discuss the threat of attacks on undersea cables and pipelines.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-the-sun-on', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-the-sun-on-potential-attacks-on-undersea-infrastructure/'}, {'signal_id': '4c846462d1991272', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The withdrawal of the US-led coalition is a loss for Iraq’s sovereignty <p>The government secured the withdrawal of foreign partners before securing obedience from armed factions. That leaves Baghdad with less leverage against Iran’s allies in Iraq.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-withdrawal-of-the-us-led-coalition-is-a-loss-for-iraqs-sovereignty/'}, {'signal_id': '95d84b6d28480cc8', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Industry groups want cyber threat-sharing law renewed through defense authorization bill Banks, utilities, and other industries are asking lawmakers to extend liability protections through 2035.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/11/industry-groups-cyber-sharing-law/416993/'}, {'signal_id': '1038e9fd6f809d7a', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Officials suspect Iran of cyberattacks on military base freezers Tehran is also suspected to have backed recent attacks on U.S. water-treatment equipment.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/11/officials-suspect-iran-series-cyberattacks-military-base-freezers/416992/'}, {'signal_id': '3c5781ba983fa480', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'The Pentagon’s IT agency wants to bridge network gaps in the Pacific “The old ways of connecting with partners are simply no longer sufficient,” says INDOPACOM deputy commander.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/technology/2026/11/pentagons-it-agency-wants-bridge-network-gaps-pacific/416963/'}, {'signal_id': '55e9f695dd5ec096', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Across the line This month’s Useful Fiction story explores how Army infantry, armor, and robotic systems might fight together.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/ideas/2026/10/across-line/416947/'}, {'signal_id': '036e16672b256b72', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Six military freezers went bad in August. Was it a cyber attack? After food spoiled at commissaries, Pentagon investigators are looking at similar incidents in France.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/10/pentagon-investigates-suspected-cyberattack-behind-military-freezer-failures/416929/'}, {'signal_id': '3c856e89d66739b9', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Army pilots are trying virtual reality to stay more alert in flight The 101st Combat Aviation Brigade is testing the NeuroTrainer as a possible readiness tool for their aviators.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/technology/2026/10/army-pilots-are-trying-virtual-reality-stay-more-alert-flight/416915/'}, {'signal_id': 'bd61e8e87f2fc7c7', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Can inertial navigation make ground-robot swarms real? Two startups are equipping small wheeled robots with a GPS-free nav package.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/defense-systems/2026/10/inertial-navigation-ground-robot-swarms/416914/'}, {'signal_id': 'bc052e87ce858512', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Defense Business Brief: Tech at the edge; PACFLEET talks cyber; and more', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/business/2026/10/defense-business-brief-tech-edge-pacfleet-talks-cyber-and-more/416906/'}, {'signal_id': 'fd23453c51268c3e', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'The US space industry will suffer for Ukraine’s Starlink outage, experts say US allies aren’t happy: “We naturally insist tha